1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,260
Ah! I slept too long!

2
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:22,000
I don't hear anything. There's no heartbeat.

3
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:24,520
It's because you're listening through his armor.

4
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,220
Looks like he finally managed to fall asleep.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,580
Suppose that means his food poisoning settled down.

6
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:35,820
Oh, Laios, what a troublemaker.

7
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:38,120
Let's let him sleep a bit longer.

8
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,760
He was tossing and turning off through the night.

9
00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:43,560
I wonder about this dungeon.

10
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:47,820
Does it already know how many monsters need to be defeated on each floor?

11
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:51,820
Killing monsters in here just stabilizes the ecosystem.

12
00:00:51,820 --> 00:00:56,240
But if we don't do it, the village will get completely overrun by them.

13
00:00:56,240 --> 00:01:00,680
And when the village does get overwhelmed, it recruits adventurers to help.

14
00:01:01,620 --> 00:01:03,620
Hmm, pretty clever system.

15
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,640
What are you talking about?

16
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:08,380
About how dungeons are made, isn't it obvious?

17
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:12,700
It was a while ago, but I studied it back when I was in school.

18
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:15,420
It's a lot more complex than you'd think.

19
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:19,480
Hey, isn't that Marcelle?

20
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:21,600
You know, from the graduate course?

21
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:24,140
She was the school's very first genius.

22
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:28,580
Yeah, I heard she was the teacher's assistant the first day.

23
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:31,960
And I heard that they've decided she's going to be a court magician.

24
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:33,680
Really? That's amazing!

25
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:34,320
Hmm.

26
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:38,740
Actually, I wasn't assisting the teacher until the fifth day of school.

27
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:41,720
And the court magician thing is because my mom was one, too.

28
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:48,220
By the way, I kind of pestered the teacher to let me join class today.

29
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:50,800
So hi. Glad to be here.

30
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:53,580
Uh, hey!

31
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:58,300
Today we're going to experiment with spirit cultivation.

32
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:01,860
I want each of you to grab a jar and head outside.

33
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:05,960
Using wooden discs with a hole in them,

34
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:10,860
place a disc and then a layer of soil on top and begin alternating.

35
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:14,220
Create a barrier over it,

36
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:17,220
and then fill the jar with mana.

37
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:20,320
Release some spirits inside.

38
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:25,840
The microscopic spirits will live off the mana in the vessel.

39
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:29,960
They'll die if the mana is too dense or too thin.

40
00:02:30,620 --> 00:02:33,520
Raising spirits is the foundation for summoning magic.

41
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:35,720
The vessel we keep them in is called a dungeonium

42
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:39,400
because it looks similar to the structure of a monster-ridden dungeon.

43
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:43,220
When you finish, place it in the dark room.

44
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:46,000
We'll see how they're doing in a week's time.

45
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:47,700
Wow!

46
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:50,400
Marcel, your barrier's so pretty!

47
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:52,760
I can't believe this was your first time!

48
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:55,740
Although, why the interest in summoning magic?

49
00:02:56,140 --> 00:02:56,360
Huh?

50
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:58,440
It's not like it's your specialty.

51
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:02,480
I've been researching things to learn how to build a safe dungeon.

52
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,240
I'm on magic ingredients now.

53
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:10,660
For example, ingredients like mandrakes are pretty dangerous to harvest.

54
00:03:12,340 --> 00:03:17,420
However, if we could create a safe dungeon that's inhabited by monsters that are useful,

55
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:20,100
then it would greatly contribute to society!

56
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:21,460
Whoa!

57
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:23,820
That sounds amazing!

58
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:25,600
Look at Marcel's barrier!

59
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:27,220
It's so enchanting!

60
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:28,700
Hey, can I see too?

61
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:30,160
Make some room for me!

62
00:03:30,780 --> 00:03:31,420
Careful!

63
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:35,780
Are you hurt?

64
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:37,920
Oh, no, I'm okay.

65
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:44,060
There are some impurities mixed in the soil.

66
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:47,520
And the mana's thin because the barrier is full of holes.

67
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:51,420
In that state, the spirits inside won't live long.

68
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:53,940
You didn't get dirt on your clothes, did you?

69
00:03:54,300 --> 00:03:54,640
Huh?

70
00:03:55,140 --> 00:04:00,140
That girl, she's always covered in dirt and ditches claths so people think she's weird.

71
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:02,120
Huh.

72
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:09,060
Now then, when everyone has their jars in front of them,

73
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:12,280
we'll see how your spirits have developed over the past week.

74
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:13,600
Are you kidding?

75
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:15,160
Mine are all dead!

76
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:16,900
Wow, mine somehow survived!

77
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:18,680
Is this a new type of spirit?

78
00:04:18,860 --> 00:04:19,860
You mean the mold?

79
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:24,820
If a good number of them survived, the fire will be large.

80
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:30,200
Looks like your spirits are being maintained nicely.

81
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:31,700
Excellent work, Marcel.

82
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:41,140
What's happening to my jar?

83
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:43,860
That's quite a lot of spirits there.

84
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,360
What do I do?

85
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:48,340
Don't worry, I'll handle it.

86
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:49,760
Please tell me!

87
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:50,820
How'd you do that?

88
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:51,720
I need to know!

89
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:57,040
Well, you see, I know a place pretty close by that has a lot of spirits.

90
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:00,840
I thought my dungeonium would work better if I used soil from there.

91
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:02,880
There's a place like that nearby?

92
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:04,460
Can you tell me where?

93
00:05:05,420 --> 00:05:07,240
Oh, it's the...

94
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:09,480
This is the same amount as in a real dungeon.

95
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:11,760
This'll be a fine sample indeed.

96
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:17,620
I got it from a real dungeon.

97
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:23,020
We can get outside from here!

98
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:26,340
This was here the whole time?

99
00:05:48,960 --> 00:05:52,060
So are you always doing stuff like this?

100
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:52,900
Yep.

101
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:57,660
That's why people think she's weird.

102
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:08,940
It's a bug!

103
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:11,260
Delicious fruit!

104
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:16,140
You can't just pick up and eat random crap you find!

105
00:06:16,260 --> 00:06:17,140
You've got to be careful!

106
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:18,820
What if those things poisoned you?

107
00:06:19,380 --> 00:06:22,000
Oh, but I actually know what these things are.

108
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:24,840
Grasshoppers and raspberries aren't poisonous.

109
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:32,740
So it really is a dungeon.

110
00:06:33,340 --> 00:06:34,380
This is amazing.

111
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:40,000
The mana here is stagnant and the air is stale.

112
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:42,440
Seems like it's a natural cave.

113
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:45,420
Wait, don't go in there!

114
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:52,220
Oh, don't worry.

115
00:06:52,860 --> 00:06:54,020
I come here often.

116
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:56,680
Stay on dry ground and it's perfectly safe.

117
00:06:56,680 --> 00:07:01,620
uh,

118
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:05,620
hmm, hmm, hmm, hmm.

119
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:13,100
Hmm.

120
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:15,340
Hmm.

121
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:16,460
Hmm.

122
00:07:16,460 --> 00:07:17,140
Hmm.

123
00:07:17,460 --> 00:07:17,880
Hmm.

124
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:18,940
Mostly.

125
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:22,480
The inside of the dungeon really is swarming with spirits, huh?

126
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,300
I took some dirt and water from here and added it to my jar.

127
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:31,440
That explains it.

128
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:33,900
So what do you come to this place to do?

129
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:38,360
I usually write letters or do some reading.

130
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:42,020
Well, they weren't wrong about her ditching class.

131
00:07:45,380 --> 00:07:48,360
Anyway, there's nothing dangerous yet.

132
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:50,060
Wait.

133
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:54,180
If we tilt this dirt and planted some mandrakes,

134
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:56,960
I think we could safely utilize the dungeon's mana.

135
00:07:58,160 --> 00:08:01,900
There's even a water source close by, so it's definitely possible.

136
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:07,760
Oh, crap! This is bad!

137
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:10,780
Just stand back! I'll get rid of this slime monster!

138
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:11,180
Wait!

139
00:08:11,540 --> 00:08:17,380
What do you think you're doing?

140
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:22,860
It won't come into the sunlight. You don't have to worry, I promise!

141
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:30,860
Slimes are actually able to break down bat droppings and then turn them into mana.

142
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:36,320
If the slimes weren't here to do that, the dungeon would die.

143
00:08:39,540 --> 00:08:40,380
Bats, huh?

144
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:42,480
Take this.

145
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:56,400
It's good.

146
00:08:56,400 --> 00:09:01,380
If they're this good, I bet the animals around here probably eat them.

147
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:06,300
I wonder what kinds of things the bats up there eat.

148
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:09,840
And what season do these raspberries grow in?

149
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:11,900
What kind of animals eat them?

150
00:09:11,900 --> 00:09:16,220
I can't make a dungeon without knowing things like that.

151
00:09:20,820 --> 00:09:23,300
I still have so much left to learn.

152
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:29,820
Thanks so much for bringing me here.

153
00:09:31,020 --> 00:09:35,780
The truth is, I thought if I'd just studied spells and magic, that was all I'd need to know.

154
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:37,580
But that's not true.

155
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:43,560
Oh, I haven't introduced myself.

156
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:45,080
My name's Valen.

157
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:47,300
Would you mind telling me your name?

158
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:56,360
My name is Marcel.

159
00:09:57,500 --> 00:10:00,320
Valen, what do you say to becoming friends?

160
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:06,380
The part about you being the school's first genius has to be a lie, right?

161
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:08,080
Why would you think it's a lie?

162
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:10,460
I'll have you know that I was an honor student.

163
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:15,560
Anyway, this whole dungeon's pretty unbelievable.

164
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:21,280
There are layers of calculations going on and tons of mana being circulated.

165
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:27,120
If the mad mage is really out there somewhere, they're not just your average magic user.

166
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:31,720
With that said, it's probably best if you stop living here, Senshi.

167
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,740
Mind your own business.

168
00:10:34,540 --> 00:10:35,020
Seriously!

169
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:36,740
You hate magic, right?

170
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:39,420
Well, the dungeon itself is entirely made out of it!

171
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:41,440
Can't hear ya.

172
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:44,100
I see.

173
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:46,640
So Valen was talking about you.

174
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:51,420
When she enrolled into magic school, she would send me update letters.

175
00:10:52,020 --> 00:10:55,360
I could tell that she was anxious there at first, but...

176
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:57,860
One day, she wrote about how she made a new friend.

177
00:10:58,520 --> 00:11:00,100
And she sounded a lot happier.

178
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:04,820
She always praised you, Marcel.

179
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:07,600
She thought you were awesome.

180
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:15,400
Valen praised you too, Laios.

181
00:11:15,620 --> 00:11:17,020
She really looked up to you.

182
00:11:17,020 --> 00:11:19,560
Is that so?

183
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:23,120
What's so great about him?

184
00:11:23,300 --> 00:11:25,740
He's got the best dog impression I've ever heard!

185
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:30,420
Maybe that's something I should keep between me and Valen for now.

186
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:35,140
Well, let's get our butts in gear and go save Valen!

187
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:38,340
Come on, you tin can!

188
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:40,620
You're awake, so get up so we can get going!

189
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:44,180
We're currently here.

190
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:48,320
The orcs we talked to mentioned the red dragon had appeared right here.

191
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:50,280
It'll take two days to get there.

192
00:11:51,160 --> 00:11:56,220
It's probably not where we left it, but dragons also aren't really the type to wander far.

193
00:11:56,780 --> 00:11:58,980
We should only make camp two more times.

194
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:03,460
First at the halfway mark, and lastly right before the dragon.

195
00:12:04,260 --> 00:12:06,460
We'll wake up Laios when the candle burns out.

196
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:08,240
Do what you need now.

197
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:10,580
We won't rest again for a while.

198
00:12:13,540 --> 00:12:14,740
I'd like to wash up.

199
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:17,000
Seriously?

200
00:12:17,620 --> 00:12:19,020
I can do it in the corner.

201
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:22,000
Just be quick about it.

202
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:28,320
We'll be outside if you need us.

203
00:12:29,460 --> 00:12:30,740
It's fine if you stay.

204
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:31,980
I'm not getting naked.

205
00:12:33,460 --> 00:12:34,700
Uh, okay.

206
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:39,300
Man, I sure do make them worry.

207
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:43,340
Wonder if I should have studied illusion magic too.

208
00:12:44,380 --> 00:12:46,060
No, that's not the problem.

209
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:49,020
It's because I'm the only girl in the party now.

210
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:52,220
We'll be parting ways here.

211
00:12:52,740 --> 00:12:53,840
Are you serious?

212
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:55,920
Does it really have to be now?

213
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:59,120
I mean, we still don't know where Valen is after all.

214
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:04,000
Sorry, but we have our own livelihoods to worry about.

215
00:13:05,680 --> 00:13:08,640
Just remembering that moment makes me mad.

216
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:10,860
I thought that we were all friends.

217
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:16,780
Wake up, Laios.

218
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:18,420
Hey, come on.

219
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:19,520
Time to get moving.

220
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:22,700
There we go.

221
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:25,840
Guess I boiled too much.

222
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:26,300
She'll be OK.

223
00:13:26,300 --> 00:13:56,280
Let's go.

224
00:13:56,300 --> 00:14:01,800
What's wrong?

225
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:05,480
What?

226
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:14,920
My water walking?

227
00:14:15,420 --> 00:14:16,460
The water's moving.

228
00:14:16,980 --> 00:14:19,280
Weapons won't work. We need fire.

229
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:20,320
Fire?

230
00:14:22,540 --> 00:14:23,840
I'll start one.

231
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:26,680
Hey, Marcel! Hold on a bit longer!

232
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:28,800
Easy for you to say.

233
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:31,560
Please let this hit it.

234
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:33,560
Come on.

235
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:52,240
Marcel!

236
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:54,460
What are you waiting for? Go!

237
00:14:55,280 --> 00:14:56,800
All of you, stay there!

238
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:59,460
My water walking spell is wearing off, so...

239
00:15:04,020 --> 00:15:07,080
Marcel!

240
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:08,480
Get up!

241
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:09,460
Keep moving!

242
00:15:09,460 --> 00:15:20,620
I won't be able to run now.

243
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:30,060
Where is it hiding?

244
00:15:38,060 --> 00:15:43,940
I can't watch! Come on, Senshi! Hurry up!

245
00:15:43,940 --> 00:15:45,780
I'm growing as fast as I can!

246
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:46,840
This is bad.

247
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:52,280
I don't have much mana left.

248
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:54,740
I've got to get it in the next shot.

249
00:16:00,780 --> 00:16:01,300
Where?

250
00:16:02,780 --> 00:16:03,920
Where is it?

251
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:06,440
There must be some kind of clue.

252
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:08,760
There!

253
00:16:10,380 --> 00:16:11,680
It has my blood!

254
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:14,020
It's so fast.

255
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:22,860
Just hold on!

256
00:16:22,860 --> 00:16:40,800
I don't talk to you!

257
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:41,780
Hey, guys?

258
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:44,520
What now?

259
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:49,260
All right, here's the plan.

260
00:16:52,340 --> 00:16:54,280
Let's get out of here!

261
00:16:56,600 --> 00:17:02,040
How are you holding up, Marcel?

262
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:06,960
I stopped the bleeding, but I'm low on blood and mana.

263
00:17:07,840 --> 00:17:09,040
So I'm spent.

264
00:17:10,220 --> 00:17:10,820
Sorry.

265
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:12,180
It's fine.

266
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:13,760
Just take it easy.

267
00:17:15,020 --> 00:17:20,040
I really should have paid more attention when Fallon was teaching me healing magic.

268
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:22,540
Hey, Laios?

269
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:25,780
What are we gonna do now?

270
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:29,740
There's no way we can take a monolith magic user further into the dungeon.

271
00:17:30,220 --> 00:17:33,620
And we can't continue on without the help of her water walking spell.

272
00:17:33,980 --> 00:17:36,000
Let's wait for other adventurers to pass by.

273
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:39,120
If we're lucky, one of them will be a healer.

274
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:43,840
There's no way that someone who's willing to help others would conveniently pass by here.

275
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:46,400
Besides, we don't have anything we can trade.

276
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:49,760
Yeah, I think the only thing we have is kelpie meat.

277
00:17:50,020 --> 00:17:51,560
Let's hope the person is starving.

278
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:54,900
It's a rare nutrient source in a dungeon.

279
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:58,160
Who cares about nutrition right now?

280
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:03,400
Actually, did you happen to grab its liver too, Senshi?

281
00:18:03,860 --> 00:18:04,780
Of course I did.

282
00:18:05,340 --> 00:18:07,580
Livers are too rich in iron to leave behind.

283
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:08,600
Hmm?

284
00:18:09,780 --> 00:18:10,080
Huh?

285
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:11,920
I knew it.

286
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:14,080
That means...

287
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:17,180
It's grilling time!

288
00:18:23,580 --> 00:18:33,620
Mane, neck, liver, ribs, tail, thigh, loin, and veggies.

289
00:18:33,620 --> 00:18:39,560
Marcelle?

290
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:41,240
Marcelle?

291
00:18:43,500 --> 00:18:44,800
You good to sit up?

292
00:18:45,660 --> 00:18:47,460
We made something nice for you.

293
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:47,500
Yeah?

294
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:48,060
Mm-hmm.

295
00:18:48,060 --> 00:19:05,020
Thigh.

296
00:19:05,840 --> 00:19:06,800
Where's the liver?

297
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:10,200
You gotta make sure organs get cooked all the way.

298
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:16,920
Forgive me, Marcelle, but I'm digging in.

299
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:18,260
Ow!

300
00:19:20,420 --> 00:19:21,600
That's pretty good.

301
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:22,700
Yeah.

302
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,880
It's a little chewy, but I like it.

303
00:19:25,340 --> 00:19:28,740
Does it taste more like a horse or a marine animal?

304
00:19:29,540 --> 00:19:32,200
I haven't eaten either, so I can't really compare it.

305
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:34,200
Ribs.

306
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:36,540
It tastes sweet, doesn't it?

307
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:38,200
Yeah, and so soft.

308
00:19:38,900 --> 00:19:40,360
Marcelle, the liver's ready now.

309
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:42,760
Tenderloin.

310
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:45,800
It's like it's melting in my mouth.

311
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:47,420
I really like this one.

312
00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:49,240
Here's some liver, Marcelle.

313
00:19:50,340 --> 00:19:50,900
Tail.

314
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:52,800
Yummy.

315
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:55,420
An interesting flavor on this one.

316
00:19:56,220 --> 00:19:56,900
Here, Marcelle.

317
00:19:57,720 --> 00:19:59,460
Have more liver, Marcelle.

318
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:01,420
How is it, Marcelle?

319
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:03,040
Eat some more, Marcelle.

320
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:04,800
You like it, Marcelle?

321
00:20:09,900 --> 00:20:10,420
Please.

322
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:14,800
Please give me the other parts, too!

323
00:20:19,940 --> 00:20:21,960
Well, it looks like she's starting to recover.

324
00:20:22,460 --> 00:20:23,580
Liver's amazing.

325
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:27,360
That aside, what do we do about her low mana?

326
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:30,480
Yeah, if only there was a meat that could help restore it.

327
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:33,040
Why'd you stuff the basilisk with monoherbs?

328
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:34,980
I still stand by my choice.

329
00:20:40,820 --> 00:20:42,140
Do you smell that?

330
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:44,560
It's coming from below.

331
00:20:44,900 --> 00:20:46,020
What is that?

332
00:20:46,520 --> 00:20:48,700
I think it's grilled meat.

333
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:51,220
Someone below must be cooking it.

334
00:20:51,220 --> 00:20:56,280
Jeez, you gotta be kidding me.

335
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:59,820
What kind of moron would be grilling meat in here?

